Fixed macOS and Windows drag-and-drop getting stuck at the screen edge, losing
the transfer after the native drag was cancelled, and failing to capture
browser image or link payloads. Prevented malformed or interrupted drag
transfers from terminating the Windows server process. Armed the Windows OLE
capture target before the cursor reaches the screen edge and waited for native
Windows and macOS payload providers before cancelling the source drag.
Consumed the synthetic cancellation mouse-up so the destination drag remains
active until the user releases the physical mouse button.
